Lombok is a popular Java library that allows you to simplify your code by automatically generating getters, setters, constructors, and more. To use Lombok for getters, you'll need to add the Lombok annotation `@Getter` to your class.

Here's an example:

Before using Lombok:
```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        this.age = age;
    }
}
```

With Lombok:
```java
import lombok.Getter;

@Getter
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

By adding the `@Getter` annotation, Lombok will automatically generate the getters for the `name` and `age` fields. You can then use these getters like this:
```java
Person person = new Person();
String name = person.getName(); // no need to write the getter method!
```

Note: You'll also need to add the Lombok plugin to your IDE (if you're using one) and the Lombok library to your project's dependencies. You can find more information on how to set up Lombok in your project on the Lombok website.

